# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# Nothing here is needed for the core loop — `wikipilot init`, `build`, and
# `serve` are fully local. A key unlocks the optional extras: init's AI
# deep-investigation pass, the ask-the-wiki assistant, and the hosted-wiki
# work in cloud/.

# --- Optional: init's AI pass and the "ask the wiki" assistant ----------------
# Read from the environment or a repo-root .env. Without it, init keeps its
# mechanical draft and the chat widget shows a setup message.
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# init's --provider flag can point the deep-investigation pass at a different
# provider. Each key below is only read when that provider is chosen at init —
# leave the ones you don't use commented out.
# Used with --provider openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Used with --provider gemini
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Used with --provider custom (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
# WIKI_INIT_API_KEY=

# Override the model init's deep-investigation pass uses.
# WIKI_INIT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Override the model the assistant uses. Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5.
# WIKI_AGENT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001


# --- Maintainer only: deploying the marketing site + cloud API ----------------
# Not needed to use or develop the CLI. `wrangler` also reads its own auth from
# `wrangler login`, which is usually easier than putting a key here.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_DNS=
# SUPABASE_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# The Worker's own secrets live in cloud/.dev.vars for local dev, and in
# `wrangler secret put` for deployed environments — not in this file.
# See cloud/README.md.
